The previous-step ownership and submit-before-post-process ordering in
deepinfer/worker/worker.py and deepinfer/worker/zos_status.py informed the bounded
native C++ adaptation in src/runtime/engine/engine_core.h and
src/runtime/contract/types.h. No Python framework, DeepSeek model mathematics,
GPU sequence-length remapping, or foreign-device kernels were copied.
NInfer retains synchronous accepted-prefix/state commit, existing stream completion,
and a single owned CPU publication step for its C1 path.
